<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sukaphaa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 1268</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sukaphaa was a Tai prince from Mong Mao in the Shan region who founded the Ahom kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assam">Assam</a>. In 1228 he crossed the Patkai hills into the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahmaputra">Brahmaputra</a> valley with his followers, and after years of moving between settlements he fixed his capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charaideo">Charaideo</a>. He absorbed the local Moran and Borahi peoples, and his dynasty ruled for six centuries. Assam marks 2 December as Sukaphaa Day.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sukaphaa.jpg" alt="Sukaphaa" width="299" height="472" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: govt of assam stamp · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sukapha.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
